{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.quincy.edu/about/work-at-qu/job-openings/#full-time-tenure-track-business-analytics-faculty-position-in-the-oakley-school-of-business": {
      "title": "Full-Time, Tenure-Track Business Analytics Faculty Position in the Oakley School of Business",
      "description": "Full-Time, Tenure-Track Business Analytics Faculty Position in the Oakley School of Business. Quincy University, a Catholic, Franciscan, and liberal arts institution emphasizing the development of servant leaders, invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position in the Oakley School of Business. Responsibilities: The primary teaching area is in the field of Business Analytics at the undergraduate level. Graduate level teaching would be based on educational and work experience. Qualifications: Required: MBA or related graduate degree. Preferred: Ph.D., D.B.A., or other terminal degree in a business area with educational background or experience with business analytics. Position Start Date: August 16, 2027 Position Salary Range: $60,000 – $75,000, based on qualifications and experience. Application Deadline: Review of applications will begin November 1, 2026. The position will remain open until it is filled. Benefits : We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes health, dental, and vision insurance; Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA); life insurance; long-term and short-term disability coverage; paid vacation, sick days, and holidays; parental leave; a 403(b) retirement plan; and tuition remission for employees and their dependents. Application Procedure: Applicants should submit a letter of application, statement of teaching philosophy, C.V, and contact information for three references to: Dr. Vicky Eidson, Dean, Oakley School of Business c/o Office of Human Resources Quincy University 1800 College Avenue Quincy, IL 62301 or hr@quincy.edu Quincy University: Founded in 1860 by Franciscan friars, Quincy University is a Catholic university emphasizing the sciences, liberal arts and the professions, integrating practical experience and Franciscan values. QU is organized into six schools, the School of Fine Arts and Communication, the Oakley School of Business, the School of Humanities, the School of Education & Human Services, the School of Science and Technology, and the President’s Honors College. Quincy University invites submissions from all qualified applicants. Individuals who have earned degrees or taught at Catholic institutions or have other experiences of working with Catholic organizations recognized by the Church and aligning with Quincy University’s mission, are especially encouraged to apply. Whether Catholic or not, the successful applicant must be able to support the Catholic and Franciscan mission of Quincy University. For more information on what this support means, please consult Ex corde Ecclesiae, the Church’s Apostolic Constitution for Catholic universities.” Faculty and advisors work with students to design customized success plans to help them graduate on time, find their passion and prepare them for life. QU is a member of NCAA Division II for intercollegiate athletics. For more information, please visit www.quincy.edu. Quincy University. Success by Design. It’s a great day to be a Hawk! Quincy, Illinois: Located in a tri-state area (Illinois, Missouri, and Iowa) on the banks of the Mississippi River, Quincy, Illinois is an affordable, family-friendly city of 40,000 residents with much to see and do! Quincy is rich in history, architecture, and cultural and recreational opportunities. St. Louis, MO is just over a 2-hour drive from Quincy. Kansas City, MO is 3 ½ hours and Quincy is 5 hours from Chicago by car. Quincy is also serviced by the Quincy Regional Airport and an Amtrak station. Employment Authorization: Employment is contingent upon a clear criminal background check. In compliance with federal law, all persons at the time of their start date will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire."
    },
    "https://www.quincy.edu/about/work-at-qu/job-openings/#full-time-faculty-positions-in-english": {
      "title": "Full -Time Faculty positions in English",
      "description": "Full -Time Faculty positions in English. Quincy University, a Catholic, Franciscan, and liberal arts institution emphasizing the development of servant leaders, invites applications for two tenure-track faculty positions in English at the rank of assistant professor or associate professor, beginning Fall 2027. Responsibilities: QU is seeking qualified candidates to teach courses in Composition, its co-requisite one-credit Writing Studio, literature, creative and technical writing, and related fields. The usual teaching load is 4 courses each semester. Academic advising and committee work are expected after the first year. The successful applicants for these positions will work cooperatively with colleagues in disciplines representing the liberal arts and the professions. Collaboration with faculty in Quincy University’s Communication program will be an expectation of our new faculty colleagues in English. Both disciplines are housed in the School of Fine Arts & Communication. Quincy University is committed to its English major and to advanced undergraduate instruction in the discipline. The successful applicants will play essential roles building enrollments through redesign of the English major. Qualifications: Specialties in any area of literature or writing are welcome. Applicants with expertise in one or more of the following areas are especially encouraged: (1) Catholic literature, including the Catholic literary canon; (2) rhetoric and composition, including business and administrative communication and science communication; (3) literature of the American Midwest. A doctoral degree in English, or a related field, with college-level teaching is preferred. Candidates with at least a Master’s degree in English, or a related field, may qualify for hire with the conversion of the position to non-tenure track. Position Start Date: August 16, 2027. Application Deadline : Review of applications will begin on September 15, 2026, and continue until the positions are filled. Salary: $50,000-$59,000, depending on experience. Benefits: We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes health, dental, and vision insurance; Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA); life insurance; long-term and short-term disability coverage; paid vacation, sick days, and holidays; parental leave; a 403(b) retirement plan; and tuition remission for employees and their dependents. Application Procedure: Send a letter of application, C.V., teaching philosophy, writing sample, example of teaching evaluations, copy of unofficial transcripts (must show all coursework completed and the conferral date of the degree), and contact information for three references to: Dr. Christine Damm Dean, School of Fine Arts & Communication c/o Office of Human Resources Quincy University 1800 College Ave. Quincy, IL 62301 or hr@quincy.edu Quincy University: Founded in 1860 by Franciscan friars, Quincy University is a Catholic university emphasizing the sciences, liberal arts and the professions. Quincy University offers 46 undergraduate programs, five master’s degrees, and a doctoral degree in Occupational Therapy, with a doctoral degree in Physical Therapy awaiting candidacy. QU is organized into six schools, the School of Fine Arts and Communication, the Oakley School of Business, the School of Humanities, the School of Education & Human Services, the School of Science and Technology, and the President’s Honors College. Quincy University invites submissions from all qualified applicants. Individuals who have earned degrees or taught at Catholic institutions or have other experiences of working with Catholic organizations recognized by the Church and aligning with Quincy University’s mission, are especially encouraged to apply. Whether Catholic or not, the successful applicant must be able to support the Catholic and Franciscan mission of Quincy University. For more information see Ex corde Ecclesiae, the Church’s Apostolic Constitution for Catholic universities. Faculty and advisors work with students to design customized success plans to help them graduate on time, find their passion and prepare them for life. QU is a member of NCAA Division II for intercollegiate athletics. For more information, please visit www.quincy.edu. Quincy University. Success by Design. It’s a great day to be a Hawk! Quincy, Illinois: Located in a tri-state area (Illinois, Missouri, and Iowa) on the banks of the Mississippi River, Quincy, Illinois is an affordable, family-friendly city of 40,000 residents with much to see and do! Quincy is rich in history, architecture, and cultural and recreational opportunities. St. Louis, MO is just over a 2-hour drive from Quincy. Kansas City, MO is 3 ½ hours and Quincy is 5 hours from Chicago by car. Quincy is also serviced by the Quincy Regional Airport and an Amtrak station. Employment Authorization : Employment is contingent upon a clear criminal background check. In compliance with federal law, all persons at the time of their start date will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire."
    },
    "https://www.quincy.edu/about/work-at-qu/job-openings/#university-registrar": {
      "title": "University Registrar",
      "description": "University Registrar. The Registrar’s Office is a strategic hub for academic policy, data integrity, technological innovation, student service, and institutional effectiveness. Quincy University, a Catholic, Franciscan, and liberal arts institution emphasizing the development of servant leaders, invites applications to serve as the institution’s next Registrar, to lead these critical efforts. Reporting to the Provost/Vice President for Academic Affairs, the Registrar is responsible for the integrity, accuracy, security, and appropriate use of academic records and provides leadership for registration, academic scheduling, grading, degree audit and conferral, transcripts and verifications, transfer credit, academic calendars, catalog and curriculum implementation, and related academic operations. This is a highly visible leadership role for a professional who can pair technical and regulatory expertise with strong judgment, collaborative leadership, and exceptional service. The successful candidate will help strengthen systems and processes, improve data quality and governance, support consistent academic policy implementation, and build productive partnerships across Academic Affairs and the University. Responsibilities: Strategic and day-to-day leadership of the Registrar’s Office and its staff, service standards, priorities, and resources. Accurate and secure academic records, registration, grading, transcripts, verifications, degree audit and conferral, transfer credit, course and classroom scheduling, academic calendars, and commencement certification. Consistent interpretation and implementation of academic policies, curriculum changes, catalog requirements, and degree rules in partnership with faculty and academic leadership. Institutional compliance related to FERPA, records privacy and retention, academic-record practices, and required enrollment/degree reporting. Functional leadership for Jenzabar J1/J1 Web Registration and related Registrar technologies, with emphasis on data integrity, thoughtful automation, testing, documentation, and process improvement. Cross-functional data stewardship and collaboration with Institutional Research, Information Technology, Admissions, Financial Aid, Athletics, Student Affairs, the Business Office, and other campus partners. A culture of accuracy, accountability, professional development, continuous improvement, and student-centered service. The Candidate: Quincy University is seeking a Registrar professional who understands both the precision of the academic record and the broader institutional impact of the Registrar’s Office. Strong candidates will bring progressively responsible higher education experience, a command of registrar operations and FERPA, comfort with complex student information systems and data, and the ability to lead people and change with clarity and professionalism. Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required. At least five years of progressively responsible experience in a Registrar’s Office, academic records, enrollment services, academic administration, or a closely related higher education function, including substantial responsibility for registrar functions. Supervisory or team leadership experience. Strong knowledge of academic records, registration, grading, degree certification, academic policy administration, and FERPA. Experience with a student information system and demonstrated ability to work effectively with data, technology, reporting, and process improvement. Excellent judgment, communication, organizational, analytical, and collaborative problem-solving skills. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s Degree preferred. Experience with Jenzabar or a comparable enterprise SIS, in a functional leadership role; experience with related catalog, transfer-articulation, workflow, degree-audit, and/or National Student Clearinghouse technologies. Prior leadership experience at a private, comprehensive university. Engagement with AACRAO, IACRAO, or another Registrar/enrollment services professional association. Budget management experience. Position Start Date: Negotiable—December 2026 / January 2027. Application Deadline: Review of applications will begin on October 30, 2026. The position will remain open until filled. Salary: $70,000 – $80,000, depending on experience. Benefits: We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes health, dental, and vision insurance; Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA); life insurance; long-term and short-term disability coverage; paid vacation, sick days, and holidays; parental leave; a 403(b) retirement plan; and tuition remission for employees and their dependents. Application Procedure: Send a letter of application, C.V./Resume, copy of unofficial transcripts (must show all coursework completed and the conferral date of the degree), and contact information for three references to: Ms. Macee Borrowman Executive Assistant to the Provost & Vice President for Academic Affairs c/o Office of Human Resources Quincy University 1800 College Ave. Quincy, IL 62301 or hr@quincy.edu Quincy University: Founded in 1860 by Franciscan friars, Quincy University is a Catholic university emphasizing the sciences, liberal arts and the professions. Quincy University offers 46 undergraduate programs, five master’s degrees, and a doctoral degree in Occupational Therapy, with a doctoral degree in Physical Therapy awaiting candidacy. QU is organized into six schools, the School of Fine Arts and Communication, the Oakley School of Business, the School of Humanities, the School of Education & Human Services, the School of Science and Technology, and the President’s Honors College. Quincy University invites submissions from all qualified applicants. Individuals who have earned degrees or worked at Catholic higher education institutions or have other experiences of working with Catholic organizations recognized by the Church and aligning with Quincy University’s mission, are especially encouraged to apply. Whether Catholic or not, the successful applicant must be able to support the Catholic and Franciscan mission of Quincy University. For more information see Ex corde Ecclesiae, the Church’s Apostolic Constitution for Catholic universities. QU is a member of NCAA Division II for intercollegiate athletics. For more information, please visit www.quincy.edu. Quincy University. Success by Design. It’s a great day to be a Hawk! Quincy, Illinois: Located in a tri-state area (Illinois, Missouri, and Iowa) on the banks of the Mississippi River, Quincy, Illinois is an affordable, family-friendly city of 40,000 residents with much to see and do! Quincy is rich in history, architecture, and cultural and recreational opportunities. St. Louis, MO is just over a 2-hour drive from Quincy. Kansas City, MO is 3 ½ hours and Quincy is 5 hours from Chicago by car. Quincy is also serviced by the Quincy Regional Airport and an Amtrak station. Employment Authorization: Employment is contingent upon a clear criminal background check. In compliance with federal law, all persons at the time of their start date will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire."
    },
    "https://www.quincy.edu/about/work-at-qu/job-openings/#major-gifts-officer-remote-hybrid-eligible": {
      "title": "Major Gifts Officer- Remote/Hybrid Eligible",
      "description": "Major Gifts Officer- Remote/Hybrid Eligible. Quincy University is seeking a Major Gifts Officer to join our Advancement team. This position may be performed remotely, with regular travel for donor and prospect meetings and periodic travel to the Quincy University campus as required. The Major Gifts Officer plays a key role in securing significant philanthropic investments to advance the strategic priorities of Quincy University. This position is responsible for identifying, qualifying, cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding major gift prospects and donors; developing a sustainable pipeline of future major gift prospects; and helping grow the University’s corporate partnership program. The Major Gifts Officer manages a portfolio of individuals, corporations, and other prospective funding partners and works collaboratively with University leadership, faculty, staff, and Advancement colleagues to align donor and partner interests with institutional priorities. Responsibilities: Develop and manage an active portfolio of approximately 100–150 major gift prospects and donors. Develop and implement strategies for the cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship of major gifts. Build strong personal relationships with prospects and donors through consistent and meaningful contact, including face-to-face meetings. Achieve established annual performance goals related to prospect qualification, donor visits, solicitations and proposals, major gift commitments, dollars raised, portfolio movement, corporate partnership development, and campaign pipeline growth. Lead the growth and development of Quincy University’s corporate partnership program. Identify, cultivate, and manage relationships with businesses and corporate partners whose interests align with University priorities. Collaborate with academic leaders, Athletics, Career Services, and other campus partners to develop opportunities involving philanthropic support, program sponsorships, scholarships, student internships and experiential learning, workforce development initiatives, in-kind support, and other mutually beneficial relationships. Identify planned giving opportunities and work with Advancement leadership and appropriate advisors to incorporate current, deferred, and blended gift strategies when appropriate. Work with University leadership, faculty, and staff to understand institutional priorities and develop compelling philanthropic and corporate partnership opportunities. Maintain accurate and detailed records of interactions with prospects and donors in the University’s donor database and prepare regular reports on portfolio activity and progress toward fundraising goals. Assist with Office of Advancement special events and other University activities. Represent Quincy University professionally and with courtesy, tact, consideration, and discretion in all interactions with the University community and the public. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Required: Bachelor’s degree in a related field. Minimum of five years of experience in major or planned gift fundraising, preferably in higher education. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Excellent interpersonal and presentation skills. Ability to understand institutional priorities and translate them into compelling philanthropic and partnership opportunities. Ability to develop and manage relationships across all levels of the University community. Ability to work successfully under pressure in a fast-paced, time-sensitive, and highly confidential environment with shifting priorities and multiple deadlines. General computer proficiency, including Microsoft Office and data management systems. Valid driver’s license. Preferred: Advanced degree. Previous fundraising experience in higher education. Work Schedule & Travel: This position requires extensive travel and a flexible work schedule. The Major Gifts Officer must be available for donor meetings, University functions, Advancement events, and other activities that may occur outside of normal business hours, including evenings and weekends. Salary: $75,000 – $90,000 Benefits: Quincy University offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes health, dental, and vision insurance; Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA); life insurance; long-term and short-term disability coverage; paid vacation, sick days, and holidays; parental leave; a 403(b) retirement plan; and tuition remission for employees and their dependents. Send letter of application, resume and three professional references to: Dan Queathem, Vice President for University Advancement c/o Office of Human Resources Quincy University 1800 College Avenue Quincy, IL 62301 hr@quincy.edu An Equal Opportunity Employer"
    },
    "https://www.quincy.edu/about/work-at-qu/job-openings/#quincy-university-security-officer": {
      "title": "Quincy University Security Officer",
      "description": "Quincy University Security Officer. The Safety & Security Department, a 24-7 operation has an immediate opening for fulltime Security Officer. Position requires sound judgement, effective communications skills, ability to walk for extended periods of time and work effectively with college age students. Previous law enforcement or security experience is preferred but not required. Responsibilities: • Serves as a representative of the University • Monitor campus door/camera security system • Unlock/lock buildings • Patrol campus perimeter • Monitor building and grounds for hazardous conditions • Make student, staff & faculty ID cards • Complete written reports • Complete other duties as assigned Qualifications: • At least 21 years of age • Valid driver’s license from the state he or she resides in • High school diploma or equivalent • Available for all shifts/flexibility in scheduling • Basic computer skills • Successful completion of background check Salary: $17.00 Benefits: We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes health, dental, and vision insurance; Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA); life insurance; long-term and short-term disability coverage; paid vacation, sick days, and holidays; parental leave; a 403(b) retirement plan; and tuition remission for employees and their dependents. Submit letter of application, resume and three references to: Robert Copley, Director of Safety & Security c/o Human Resources Quincy University 1800 College Ave. Quincy, IL 62301 or hr@quincy.edu An Equal Opportunity Employer"
    },
    "https://www.quincy.edu/about/work-at-qu/job-openings/#student-financial-services-counselor": {
      "title": "Student Financial Services Counselor",
      "description": "Student Financial Services Counselor. Quincy University seeks qualified applicants for a full-time Student Financial Services Counselor. Responsibilities: Serving as a counselor and advisor to students and their families as they consider options to finance a Quincy University education. One is expected to understand all federal, state, and University funding options. Student Financial Services counselors are expected to assist students with understanding and filing the Free Application for Federal Student Aid (FAFSA), explain the awarding process and ensure financial aid awards are delivered timely and accurately. All members of the staff are expected to develop expertise required to provide assistance in all areas of office operations. Counselors provide counseling in area of loan default prevention and financial literacy, responsible for loan origination and reconciliation, ensure awarded loans meet federal requirements and timely delivery of funds to students. Qualifications: While a Bachelor’s degree is preferred, an Associate’s degree is required with two or three years of experience in a financial aid office are required for consideration. Positive attitude Excellent written/verbal communication skills with the ability to provide timely and accurate information. Applicant must be detail-oriented and computer literate. Must pass federal financial aid officer training program (online). Salary: $17.00 hr Benefits: Includes medical, dental, vision, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, long- and short-term disability coverage, paid holidays, 403(b) retirement plan, tuition remission for undergraduate tuition for employees and dependents and graduate tuition for employees, as well as vacation and sick leave benefits in accordance with university policy. Send letter of application, resume and three professional references to: Tom Oliver, VP for Enrollment and Sr. Director of Student Financial Services c/o Office of Human Resources Quincy University 1800 College Ave. Quincy, IL 62301 or hr@quincy.edu An Equal Opportunity Employer"
    },
    "https://www.quincy.edu/about/work-at-qu/job-openings/#assistant-softball-coach": {
      "title": "Assistant Softball Coach",
      "description": "Assistant Softball Coach. Quincy University, a NCAA Division II institution and member of the Great Lakes Valley Conference, invites applications for the position of Assistant Softball Coach. Responsibilities: • Serves as a representative of the University, promoting QU’s mission, image and goals to colleagues and the community. • All aspects of recruitment including – scouting perspective student athletes, organizing staff recruiting calendar schedules, and the coordination of on campus recruit visits. • Assists in coaching, and training student athletes • Assist and coordinate with camp & clinics • Assist in field and facility maintenance • Perform other duties assigned by the Head Coach Qualifications: • Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree preferred. • Prior coaching or playing experience preferred. • Valid driver’s license with good driving record • Strong communication, leadership, and organizational skills Salary: $30,000 – $33,000 depending on experience Benefits: We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes health, dental, and vision insurance; Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA); life insurance; long-term and short-term disability coverage; paid vacation, sick days, and holidays; parental leave; a 403(b) retirement plan; and tuition remission for employees and their dependents. Send letter of application, resume and three professional references to: McKendree Ward, Head Softball Coach c/o Office of Human Resources Quincy University 1800 College Ave. Quincy, IL 62301 or hr@quincy.edu An Equal Opportunity Employer"
    }
  },
